Section: 1.2. CI
Text: 1.2. CI CI is another primary type of Chinese poetry. In contrast to SHI, CI has nearly one thousand forms. Each form of CI (it is called Cipai scholarly) is deﬁned by a ﬁxed number of lines for the poem and, a ﬁxed number of characters for a particular line which usually varies for different lines.

