=== Generated Answer (model draft; check against evidence) ===
The paper generates Chinese classical poems of two primary categories: SHI (specifically Jueju and Lvshi) and CI (121 major Cipai forms).

The proposed uniformed framework uses a single GPT-2 based model to generate major types of Chinese classical poems, covering the two major SHI forms, Jueju and Lvshi, as well as 121 major forms (Cipai) of CI [1][9]. SHI and CI are the two primary categories of Chinese classical poetry, with 92.87% of poems in CCPC1.0 belonging to SHI and 7.13% to CI [5]. CI itself has nearly one thousand forms, each (called Cipai) defined by a fixed number of lines and a fixed number of characters per line [2].
